 "label_basis": "agents/retrain-policy.md judges against the current production configuration (seed 0). Variant add: overall MSE -0.21% (-0.73 to 0.26), storm -0.66% (-4.82 to 4.53). Variant replace: overall +0.35% (-0.11 to 0.84), storm +1.31% (-2.86 to 6.96). No claimed gain has an interval that excludes zero and neither reaches 2% overall or 3% storm, so the bar is not met. The 3 seed averages agree: overall -0.01% for both variants, storm +0.42% (add) and -0.87% (replace), all intervals include zero.",
 "reading": [
  "Clean validation, seed 0, add: all: seed 0 MSE -0.21% (-0.73 to 0.26); quiet (Dst > -50): seed 0 MSE -0.18% (-0.55 to 0.19); storm (Dst <= -50): seed 0 MSE -0.66% (-4.82 to 4.53); intense (Dst <= -100): seed 0 MSE -7.26% (-14.62 to 12.93).",
  "Clean validation, seed 0, replace: all: seed 0 MSE +0.35% (-0.11 to 0.84); quiet (Dst > -50): seed 0 MSE +0.27% (-0.16 to 0.72); storm (Dst <= -50): seed 0 MSE +1.31% (-2.86 to 6.96); intense (Dst <= -100): seed 0 MSE -2.91% (-10.88 to 7.62).",
  "Intense hours (35) move by -5% to -6% on the 3 seed average for both variants, but the intervals include zero and 3.9% of the block resamples hold no intense hour at all (dropped from those intervals); not evidence.",
  "As the issue expected for clean OMNI, the windows are neutral: the exact lags 0 to 5 already let the trees form the 2 and 3 hour extremes. Whether they help under real-time timing errors was not measured in this run.",
  "The code stays behind an option that is off by default."
